Sorry for the long silence here. Before rebasing, could you say more about the setup? If each routing key can be bound to its own queue, you can configure one transport per queue with its own `serializer`, and the message class follows from the transport rather than the routing key. If the payload carries a type field, a custom serializer can pick the class from the body.

The routing key only becomes necessary if a wildcard binding funnels several keys into one queue and the body has no discriminator. If that is your case, tell us, because then the right fix is not an `extra` key in the decode payload but giving the serializer typed access to the stamps the receiver already builds (`AmqpReceivedStamp` carries the full `\AMQPEnvelope`). If one of the first two works for you, let's close this.

